## Error Response DTOs

```java
// Standard error response:
public class ApiError {
    private int status;
    private String errorCode;      // Machine-readable: "ORDER_NOT_FOUND"
    private String message;        // Human-readable: "Order with ID 42 was not found"
    private String path;           // Request URI: "/api/orders/42"
    private Instant timestamp;
    private String requestId;      // Correlation ID from MDC
    private List<FieldError> fieldErrors;  // For validation failures

    @Data
    public static class FieldError {
        private String field;         // "items[0].quantity"
        private String message;       // "must be greater than 0"
        private Object rejectedValue; // The value that was rejected
    }

    public static ApiError of(int status, String errorCode, String message,
                               HttpServletRequest request) {
        ApiError error = new ApiError();
        error.status = status;
        error.errorCode = errorCode;
        error.message = message;
        error.path = request.getRequestURI();
        error.timestamp = Instant.now();
        error.requestId = MDC.get("requestId");  // From correlation ID filter
        return error;
    }
}

// Spring Boot 3 built-in ProblemDetail (RFC 7807):
ProblemDetail problem = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(
    HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "Order not found: " + id);
problem.setType(URI.create("https://api.example.com/errors/order-not-found"));
problem.setTitle("Order Not Found");
problem.setProperty("requestId", MDC.get("requestId"));
return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(problem);
```

## Centralized Exception Handler

```java
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

    // 400 - Validation errors (JSON request body)
    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleValidation(
            MethodArgumentNotValidException ex, HttpServletRequest request) {

        List<ApiError.FieldError> fieldErrors = ex.getBindingResult().getFieldErrors()
            .stream()
            .map(fe -> {
                ApiError.FieldError error = new ApiError.FieldError();
                error.setField(fe.getField());
                error.setMessage(fe.getDefaultMessage());
                error.setRejectedValue(fe.getRejectedValue());
                return error;
            })
            .collect(Collectors.toList());

        ApiError apiError = ApiError.of(400, "VALIDATION_FAILED",
            "Request validation failed", request);
        apiError.setFieldErrors(fieldErrors);
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body(apiError);
    }

    // 400 - Validation errors (path vars, query params)
    @ExceptionHandler(ConstraintViolationException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleConstraintViolation(
            ConstraintViolationException ex, HttpServletRequest request) {
        List<ApiError.FieldError> fieldErrors = ex.getConstraintViolations()
            .stream()
            .map(cv -> {
                ApiError.FieldError error = new ApiError.FieldError();
                error.setField(cv.getPropertyPath().toString());
                error.setMessage(cv.getMessage());
                error.setRejectedValue(cv.getInvalidValue());
                return error;
            })
            .collect(Collectors.toList());

        ApiError apiError = ApiError.of(400, "VALIDATION_FAILED",
            "Invalid request parameters", request);
        apiError.setFieldErrors(fieldErrors);
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body(apiError);
    }

    // 404 - Not Found
    @ExceptionHandler(EntityNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleNotFound(
            EntityNotFoundException ex, HttpServletRequest request) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
            .body(ApiError.of(404, "NOT_FOUND", ex.getMessage(), request));
    }

    // 409 - Business conflict
    @ExceptionHandler(BusinessConflictException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleConflict(
            BusinessConflictException ex, HttpServletRequest request) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT)
            .body(ApiError.of(409, ex.getErrorCode(), ex.getMessage(), request));
    }

    // 415 - Unsupported media type
    @ExceptionHandler(HttpMediaTypeNotSupportedException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleUnsupportedMediaType(
            HttpMediaTypeNotSupportedException ex, HttpServletRequest request) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE)
            .body(ApiError.of(415, "UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE",
                "Content-Type '" + ex.getContentType() + "' is not supported", request));
    }

    // 500 - Unexpected errors
    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleUnexpected(
            Exception ex, HttpServletRequest request) {
        log.error("Unexpected error on {} {}: {}",
            request.getMethod(), request.getRequestURI(), ex.getMessage(), ex);
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)
            .body(ApiError.of(500, "INTERNAL_ERROR",
                "An unexpected error occurred. Reference: " + MDC.get("requestId"),
                request));
    }
}
```

## Correlation ID Filter

```java
@Component
public class CorrelationIdFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {

    private static final String REQUEST_ID_HEADER = "X-Request-ID";
    private static final String MDC_KEY = "requestId";

    @Override
    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request,
                                     HttpServletResponse response,
                                     FilterChain chain) throws IOException, ServletException {
        String requestId = Optional.ofNullable(request.getHeader(REQUEST_ID_HEADER))
            .filter(id -> !id.isBlank())
            .orElse(UUID.randomUUID().toString());

        MDC.put(MDC_KEY, requestId);
        response.setHeader(REQUEST_ID_HEADER, requestId);  // Echo back to client

        try {
            chain.doFilter(request, response);
        } finally {
            MDC.remove(MDC_KEY);
        }
    }
}

// Log entries automatically include requestId:
// {"timestamp":"...","requestId":"abc-123","level":"ERROR","message":"..."}
// Client sees X-Request-ID: abc-123 in response
// Support can look up abc-123 in log aggregator → full request trace
```

## Production Reality

Use Spring Boot 3's `application.properties` to enable Problem Details globally:
```
spring.mvc.problemdetails.enabled=true
```
This makes Spring's built-in exceptions (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`, `HttpMediaTypeNotSupportedException`, etc.) automatically return RFC 7807 format. You only need to handle your custom business exceptions in `@RestControllerAdvice`. Every API error response must include the request ID — without it, production debugging is nearly impossible.
